## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: crs, Language: Seselwa Creole French, Number of verses: 21
## References: Bonan, C. (2013). The core grammar of Guadeloupean Creole: A descriptive and comparative approach [Master’s thesis, Ca’ Foscari University of Venice]. Università Ca’ Foscari Venezia. https://unitesi.unive.it/retrieve/37222082-c842-4449-b0c8-5ed33507c3bd/823195-1173889.pdf ; Haspelmath, M., & Tadmor, U. (Eds.). (2020). World Loanword Database (WOLD). Max Planck Institute for Evolutionary Anthropology. https://wold.clld.org/vocabulary/7
